{"kind":"request","text":"Sales slice C1: the marketing calendar, in the test host\n\nLane D under lanes act 2fb33eb1. Start from current main. S4 is landing now, so merge main again before review.\n\nThe marketing calendar is the first of the three sales applications in notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md, section 7. It needs only today's forms and today's publication to a Git destination. Slice C1 in section 8 is this request, at about two days.\n\nBuild it as a package on the grow room's forms, the way the grow and lending applications are built:\n1. Definitions: the owner, reviewer and writer members; the grants publish.plan, publish.write, publish.approve and publish.send; and the items campaign, post and comment, with the post states in section 7.\n2. Rules: an unapproved post two days before its date reaches the owner's carousel. A post past its date and not admitted reaches it too.\n3. Views: the owner's calendar carousel, the post card (Approve, and Publish when approved), the campaign record, and the log of admitted publications with checks by name.\n4. Publication: publish sends the approved text to the site's Git destination as publish-file. The publish send's result clause writes the post's request outcome: admitted, refused with the reason, or superseded. Superseded returns the post to approved.\n5. A scenario in the test host that runs the steps below.\n\nDone when, in the test host:\n- a planned post is drafted, approved at its exact revision, published to a test destination and admitted, and a member's check is recorded by name;\n- a revise after approval resets the approval;\n- a refused result leaves the post refused with its reason;\n- an unapproved post two days before its date reaches the owner's carousel;\n- a twenty-fifth post and a text over four kibibytes are refused by name.\n\nWrite an implementation note that names the forms the package uses and anything it needed beyond them. Update docs/roadmap.md or docs/use-cases.md where the calendar now runs. If a step needs a design decision or a change to a shared package, stop and bring the question to the planner before you write that source.\n\nC4 covers hosting and a homepage page. This slice does neither.","body":{"conditions":"One head on a pushed builder branch that contains current main. Tests for the done-when facts only. One npm run gate before review, in the single validation slot, after M0's and the formal candidate's gates. No live room, deployment or mini access. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","target_head":"871df9a979bc68ecadef7ef4e618cc0bcef4a97c","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}